# Linear feature ticket

## How to use

Create or update an issue with `save_issue`. Put this body in `description`. A feature is a new capability. Use the improvement template when the work changes something that already exists.

- `priority`: `1` Urgent, `2` High, `3` Medium, or `4` Low. Use `3` unless the user states otherwise.
- `addLabels`: an existing label from `list_issue_labels`.
- `blockedBy` and `relatedTo`: only issues the user names.
- `project`: the epic's project name, id, or `P-ENG-123` when the feature belongs to one.
- `estimate`: set only when the user supplies a number.

Write a title that names the capability. Delete any section below that does not apply.

## Body

```markdown
## Summary

[What problem this solves, and for whom.]

## Requirements

- [Testable behavior.]
- [Testable behavior.]

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] [Functional outcome.]
- [ ] [Edge case or failure outcome.]
- [ ] [Performance, accessibility, or security outcome, when the change needs one.]

## Technical notes

[Constraints, existing modules, or design links. Omit when there are none.]

## Testing

- [ ] Automated tests cover the new behavior.
- [ ] Manual check: [the user flow to try.]

## Out of scope

- [Behavior this issue does not include.]
```
